<section class="rag-lab" data-rag-lab aria-label="Try retrieval context">
  <p class="rag-lab__eyebrow">INTERACTIVE · Fictional policy example</p>
  <p class="rag-lab__question"><strong>Question:</strong> Who can approve a production release?</p>
  <fieldset>
    <legend>Choose what information the model receives</legend>
    <label><input type="radio" name="rag-context" value="none" checked /> No retrieved text</label>
    <label><input type="radio" name="rag-context" value="relevant" /> Current, relevant policy</label>
    <label><input type="radio" name="rag-context" value="irrelevant" /> Irrelevant document</label>
  </fieldset>
  <div class="rag-lab__panel" data-rag-panel="none">
    <p class="rag-lab__label">Retrieved context</p>
    <p>No source passages were provided.</p>
    <p class="rag-lab__label">Illustrative cautious answer</p>
    <blockquote>I can't confirm who approves production releases without an applicable policy.</blockquote>
    <p class="rag-lab__lesson">No evidence? A responsible system can abstain rather than guess.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="rag-lab__panel" data-rag-panel="relevant" hidden>
    <p class="rag-lab__label">Retrieved context · fictional current policy</p>
    <p>“Production deployment requires sign-off from the release manager and the security reviewer after staging checks pass.” <strong>[release-policy.md, current]</strong></p>
    <p class="rag-lab__label">Illustrative grounded answer</p>
    <blockquote>The release manager and security reviewer must both sign off after staging checks pass. [release-policy.md]</blockquote>
    <p class="rag-lab__lesson">Now there is inspectable evidence, but a real application must check freshness, authorization and whether the answer follows the source.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="rag-lab__panel" data-rag-panel="irrelevant" hidden>
    <p class="rag-lab__label">Retrieved context · fictional incident note</p>
    <p>“When an outage cannot be restored, on-call staff contact the incident commander.” <strong>[incidents.md]</strong></p>
    <p class="rag-lab__label">Illustrative cautious answer</p>
    <blockquote>This document describes incident escalation, not deployment approvals. I can't answer from it.</blockquote>
    <p class="rag-lab__lesson">Retrieval happened, but it found the wrong material. An irrelevant citation cannot rescue an answer.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="rag-lab__disclaimer">This is a deterministic explanation, not live inference. Nothing is transmitted to an AI service.</p>
  <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to switch examples. The initial no-context example remains visible.</p></noscript>
</section>
<script>
  for (const lab of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-rag-lab]')) {
    const radios = lab.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="rag-context"]');
    const panels = lab.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-rag-panel]');
    function update() {
      const selected = [...radios].find((radio) => radio.checked)?.value ?? 'none';
      for (const panel of panels) panel.hidden = panel.dataset.ragPanel !== selected;
    }
    for (const radio of radios) radio.addEventListener('change', update);
    update();
  }
</script>
